From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Dice <joel.dice@akamai.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Feb 2026 10:21:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] use `sys/ioctl.h` in `socketmodule.c` on WASI

As of this writing, `wasi-libc` does not yet support `O_NONBLOCK` in its `fcntl`
implementation, but _does_ support `FIONBIO` in its `ioctl` implementation, so
we need to use the latter.
---
 Modules/socketmodule.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Modules/socketmodule.c b/Modules/socketmodule.c
index b9dadaf6a8..4997518ac2 100644
--- a/Modules/socketmodule.c
+++ b/Modules/socketmodule.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ shutdown(how) -- shut down traffic in one or both directions\n\
 # define USE_GETHOSTBYNAME_LOCK
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__CYGWIN__) || defined(__NetBSD__)
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__CYGWIN__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__wasi__)
 #  include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #endif
 
